WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.630
I've always been kind of
a doodler and a drawer.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.810
Two years ago when I
was working at an agency

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:30.290
in the city, I made my
CEO a pair of sneakers.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.540
It kind of grew from there.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.080
I always was this female
thinker and creator

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.100
in this male space that I said to myself,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.600
why can't the two be together?

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.300
Being connected on Instagram and online

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.750
has enhanced my work, my visibility,

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.767
and it's enhanced my
ability to collaborate.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:08.410
The questionnaire really
simplifies the way that I design.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:12.120
It's essentially things I
would naturally ask a friend

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.703
of mine if I were
designing their sneakers.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.840
When I start drawing
on a sneaker, I like to

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:32.440
incorporate the curves
into my work rather than

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:37.190
trying to fit in a certain
design within a certain space.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.190
What I love about art, and about

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:47.190
the sneaker world in general,
is that it's colorful,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.620
it's energetic, it has to do with sport,

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.040
but it also has to do with aesthetics.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.780
But I think that people
really remember my work

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.380
because they see this unique hybrid,

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.372
and it resonates with a lot of people.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.060
Taking small steps toward your
goals can have a huge impact.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.640
Taking little steps to
where you want to go

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.632
is way better than not trying at all.

